Id: lin035f
Severity: FAIL
Category: network
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set net.ipv6.conf.all.accept_source_route=0 and .default.accept_source_route=0 in /etc/sysctl.d.
References: sysctl.d(5); Linux kernel ip-sysctl documentation
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

net.ipv6.conf.*.accept_source_route is 1, so the host accepts IPv6
packets that dictate their own route. See lin016f for the IPv4
equivalent:
  # sysctl -w net.ipv6.conf.all.accept_source_route=0
  # sysctl -w net.ipv6.conf.default.accept_source_route=0
